<section id="now">
<div class="wrap">
<div class="sec-head"><div class="sec-k"><span class="sn">16</span>Where are they now</div><h2 class="rv">The afterlife</h2></div>
<div class="now-grid">
<div class="now rv"><div class="st" style="color:var(--gold)">Reincarnated</div><h3>The sock puppet</h3><p>Hakan Enterprises bought the rights for <b>$125,000</b> in 2001.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-17">17</a></sup> In May 2002 it became the spokes-dog for 1-800-BarNone, a car-loan company for people with bad credit: “Everyone deserves a second chance.”<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-18">18</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st" style="color:var(--blue)">Acquired</div><h3>The domain</h3><p>PetSmart.com paid <b>$375,000</b> for the domain names, trademarks and related IP: $225K on signing and $150K at closing.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-6">6</a></sup> By February 2001, pets.com welcomed visitors to PETsMART.com.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-36">36</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st" style="color:var(--red)">Buried</div><h3>The company</h3><p>Renamed IPET Holdings, with Richard G. Couch as sole director, based in Danville, CA.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-6">6</a></sup> The proxy had estimated “up to approximately $0.25” a share<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-24">24</a></sup>. Holders got $0.172 in total, and the registration ended in 2005.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-23">23</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st" style="color:var(--mute)">Written off</div><h3>Amazon’s stake</h3><p>About 30% as of Oct 31, 2000. A spokeswoman said its value was “down to zero.”<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-11">11</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st" style="color:var(--mute)">Dispersed</div><h3>The 320 employees</h3><p>About 255 were laid off on Nov 7, 2000.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-5">5</a></sup> The 26 who were left at year-end resigned after the January 2001 vote.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-6">6</a></sup></p></div>
<div class="now rv"><div class="st" style="color:var(--green)">Vindicated</div><h3>The idea</h3><p>Chewy did $11.86B in FY2024 net sales, nearly 80% of it from Autoship subscriptions.<sup class="fn"><a href="#src-19">19</a></sup></p></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

